From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:14:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mfplat: Close a file byte stream's file in Close().

It returned E_NOTIMPL and kept the file open until the last reference
went, so a file written through the MP4 sink could not be opened
exclusively right after the sink writer finalized it, as it can on
Windows (mfreadwrite's test_sink_writer_sample_process).  Close() now
closes the file and can be called again, as the stream-based byte
stream's already can (test_bytestream_from_stream).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/mfplat/main.c b/dlls/mfplat/main.c
index ae3219084e2..573aba73ba5 100644
--- a/dlls/mfplat/main.c
+++ b/dlls/mfplat/main.c
@@ -4202,9 +4202,19 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI bytestream_file_Flush(IMFByteStream *iface)
 
 static HRESULT WINAPI bytestream_file_Close(IMFByteStream *iface)
 {
-    FIXME("%p\n", iface);
+    struct bytestream *stream = impl_from_IMFByteStream(iface);
 
-    return E_NOTIMPL;
+    TRACE("%p.\n", iface);
+
+    EnterCriticalSection(&stream->cs);
+    if (stream->hfile)
+    {
+        CloseHandle(stream->hfile);
+        stream->hfile = NULL;
+    }
+    LeaveCriticalSection(&stream->cs);
+
+    return S_OK;
 }
 
 static HRESULT WINAPI bytestream_SetCurrentPosition(IMFByteStream *iface, QWORD position)
